	--REMEMBER:
		--FSO uses LUA 5.1 
		--small ship waves don't have gcw ship entries (ie Alpha B 5...) so use function to get parent then refer to that parent for any GCW table updates/checks
		--hyper-parameters values should never be decimals since math.random() only uses integers
		--subsystems uses submodel name in lua table structure, but `.Name` calls/sets the display name. 
			--ship.Engine_LeftA.HitpointsLeft is valid and does not change and is correct usage 
			--though note that ship.Engine_LeftA.Name gives 'Engine (left)', which when trying to call from ship[ss_name] will not be valid
			--to use name of subsystem in sexp use `tostring(subsystem.CanonicalName)`
		--`On Gameplay Start` runs properly even with quick restarts
		--`On State End` of State GAMEPLAY only runs with the mission is over it seems, even if paused or in menu..
			--..`On State Start` runs each time coming back into game from a menu though
		--update GCW version if json file structure changed in any way
		--DO NOT use 'arg or true' for boolean arguments to functions, since it makes false args true
		--VS Code: mouse button back goes to last location; CTR R runs file; CRT SHIFT R clears output
		--Usually use LUA VS code extension from Tencent, also 
			--use ZeroBrane to check for errors (shift f7) and 
			--Sumneko LUA VS code extension for more error catching (it's slow at auto-filling though and not as good at navigation "self")
		--string.find() doesn't work with certain characters like dashes (-) or periods (.). The full list is https://www.lua.org/pil/20.2.html
			--..It does work with colons (:) and hashtags (#) and underscores (_). 
			--..If dashes or periods or others are needed use '%.' IE matches a dot. See https://www.lua.org/pil/20.2.html for more details. 
		--some big ship orders will give a remove all orders if there are no valid targets
		--to remove a string key value from table set it to nil, but to remove number use table.remove
		--do not set tables equal to each other!!
			--if local t = global tbl then changes to t will affect both t and tbl, but if only single value changing then changes in t will not affect tbl
		--functions and base of global vars use caps, others like vars use lowercase
		--locals in various states are local whenever that stuff in that state is used, but not outside of that state

		--For Docking: Questions and Answers of Current FSO 25.0

			--can dock while mothership is moving?
			--  ship will do dock paths where snapshot of mothership used to be, and then will slide to try and match current mothership position in final dock path
			--if docked and mothership blows up what happens?
			--  small ship undocks and resumes just normally flying around
			--if told to dock and mothership blows up what happens?
			--  small ship stops order and resumes just flying around

			--if AI is attacking any ship or specific ship, and ship comes under 'protected' status or changes to non hostile IFF:
			--  the ship will stop attack and just sit next to it if attack any if not previously attacking, 
			--    but continue attacking if ordered for specific ship or was already attacking as part of attack any
			--  if non hostile IFF, player can still order wingmen to attack it as specific ship, but attack any they will not
			--  only time a friendly ship will stop attacking other team ship is if it is Friendly IFF (no other team triggers this)

			--if given order by player to attack/disable protected ship, AI will say yes
			--  ai will say yes and actually attack it and unprotect it, but only if it is a fighter/bomber or freighter or transport
			--  actually seems to attack regardless of ship type, though not unprotect it

			--clearing orders while docked is fine
			--clearing orders while docking is fine
			--clearing orders while undocking is stops the undocking and snaps back docked position
			--adding higher priority dock or un-dock orders while docking or undocking does nothing and lets both keep going as they were
			--adding higher priority waypoint order while docking stops the docking and ship follows waypoint
			--adding higher priority waypoint order while undocking allows undocking to continue then ship follows waypoint once undocking done


			--How to Deal with in PA
			--
			--recall, protected flag can be removed by player order to attack a ship, so only use for non 'fighter' 'bomber' 'transport' 'freighter'
			--mtype-> big ship bool, is_target_for_boarding = false or true
			--if true, then protect-ship and add guardian threshold and lock weapons and set all turrets to 0 health so they do not appear
			--  and also prevent engines from repairing while mission ongoing (engines only repair if mission over, so player can see ship leave)
			--  in code 'protect-ship' ensures attack-any does not work and in the lua orders we do not allow bombers or other ships to attack this target to death
			--  fortunately this also makes more sense to player, as that way they can still order their wingmen to disable something

			--when arrive, order to follow and face, when target disabled then order dock
			--when ordered to dock add to table, then update on battle status update if docked, when time up then update order 
			--  when doing dock order, make sure no other friendly ship is already docking with this ship
			--  also once docked protect boarding ship? yes since otherwise would damage boardee, then unprotect once undocked

			--Issue, I want to board ship A, but it leaves, and now I want to see if I can board ship B b/c the my friend who was going to board b has died before being able to board it successfully. 
			-- Recall, if I have a retreat order it takes highest PR and I cannot do any boarding.
			-- So when ship leaves it triggers big ship orders, and any big ship that had that ship as a target will re-run current orders to find new target.
			--  If stalking then that's fine, we will get a new target.
			--  If boarding that is also fine, as we will run our docking order, see our target is not valid, then trigger the stalking order.

			-- use boarding tracker table, see NAV_HELP 9876

			--recall these functions exist:
			--  Movements:DockOrderSafe( and Movements:UndockOrderSafe(
			--  number :numDocked()
			--  boolean :isDocked(


